Subject: Conversation Work Attribution Canonical SJS Specification
Date: 2026-05-14
Description: Signed canonical authority for attributing work to persistent Codex conversation identities during concurrent AlienHand development.

@ [source_seed] AlienHand/docs/sjs/source/2026-05-14-conversation-work-attribution/source-seed.sop
@ [sjs_protocol] platform/refinement/Specification_Justification_Solution.sop
@ [spec_governance] platform/refinement/Specification_Governance.sop
@ [data_driven_design] platform/refinement/Data_Driven_Design.sop

& [CanonicalRecord: ConversationWorkAttribution] is the processed implementation authority
  + [source_document] is AlienHand/docs/sjs/source/2026-05-14-conversation-work-attribution/source-seed.sop
  + [canonical_source_specification] is this document
  + [authority_scope] is conversation identity, work ownership, dirty worktree attribution, SJS justification linkage, and concurrent-agent coordination
  + [satisfaction_signature] is [SatisfactionSignature: ConversationWorkAttribution]

  = must: assign one persistent [conversation_uuid] for each active Codex conversation that mutates or plans to mutate project work
  = must: record the [conversation_uuid] in a conversation record before or with the next coherent implementation slice
  = must: include [conversation_uuid] in future SJS justification records when work is implemented from that conversation
  = must: classify dirty files as owned, foreign, mixed, unknown, or generated before staging or editing them
  = must: avoid claiming authorship for uncommitted work unless the conversation record, staged diff, commit, or justification evidence supports that claim
  = must: preserve uncertainty explicitly when authorship cannot be proven
  = must: keep source user statements separate from canonical policy records

& [ConversationIdentityContract] is the persistent identity rule
  + [conversation_uuid] is a UUID assigned to one Codex conversation thread
  + [conversation_label] is a short human-readable name for the current workstream
  + [workspace_scope] is the repository or directory set the conversation may touch
  + [active_scope] is the files, modules, specs, or subsystems presently owned by the conversation
  + [handoff_note] is a concise summary another conversation can inspect before touching overlapping work

  = must: keep [conversation_uuid] stable across compaction and follow-up turns in the same conversation
  = must: record new coherent slices in SJS justification with the same [conversation_uuid]
  = must: update [active_scope] or create a handoff note when the conversation changes subsystem focus

& [DirtyWorktreeAttributionContract] is the concurrent-work safety rule
  + [owned] means the current conversation has direct evidence it produced the dirty change
  + [foreign] means another conversation, user process, generated output, or external tool likely produced the dirty change
  + [mixed] means the file contains both current-conversation and non-current-conversation changes
  + [unknown] means authorship cannot be determined from available evidence
  + [generated] means the file is build, proof, runtime, cache, or tool output

  = must: inspect a dirty file before editing or staging it
  = must: stage only owned hunks or agreed mixed hunks for a coherent commit
  = must: record unresolved authorship as unknown rather than assuming ownership
  = must: stop and ask for direction if a foreign or unknown dirty change directly blocks the current implementation
  = should: use separate commits per coherent conversation-owned slice
  = should: prefer SJS justification entries over prose-only memory when work may be reviewed later

& [JustificationAugmentationContract] is the SJS linkage rule
  + [field] is conversation_uuid
  + [field] is conversation_label
  + [field] is worktree_attribution
  + [field] is dirty_file_policy

  = must: include [conversation_uuid] in future implementation justification records
  = should: include [worktree_attribution] when dirty worktree overlap was observed
  = should: identify files intentionally not touched because ownership was foreign, mixed, generated, or unknown

& [CurrentConversationBootstrap] is the first assigned conversation identity under this policy
  + [conversation_uuid] is 7600f77c-9365-4901-ba2a-0250757acb3f
  + [conversation_label] is codex-stream-worker-and-chat-platform
  + [workspace_scope] is C:\Project\Codex_Projects\ReasoningFramework\AlienHand
  + [initial_reason] is this conversation discovered ambiguous dirty worktree attribution around AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/cli.py

  = must: use this UUID for future SJS justification entries from this conversation unless the user explicitly starts a new conversation identity

& [SatisfactionSignature: ConversationWorkAttribution] is the valid SJS satisfaction signature
  + [signature_protocol_uuid] is ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
  + [signature_uuid] is 5d5d6fce-d8ff-46ee-85f3-0c6fd8f711fb
  + [signed_subject] is AlienHand/docs/sjs/canonical/conversation-work-attribution.canonical.sop
  + [source_specification] is AlienHand/docs/sjs/source/2026-05-14-conversation-work-attribution/source-seed.sop
  + [canonical_source_specification] is AlienHand/docs/sjs/canonical/conversation-work-attribution.canonical.sop
  + [processed_stage_set] is source_preserved, delineated, semantically_refined, constraint_checked, justified, solution_seeded, and registry_recorded
  + [signature_status] is valid
  + [invalidation_condition] is source_change, missing_conversation_uuid, conflicting_conversation_identity, broken_lineage, or implementation_contradiction

  = must: identify this file as the processed AlienHand conversation work attribution policy
